For your question ("Do males and females differ in how immune genes are co-regulated once body length and lake are taken into account?"), these fit best, and here is why:
- **COBRA** — Put the group label in COBRA's design matrix: it returns a co-expression component for that variable -- the part of each gene pair's co-expression associated with the group -- alongside components for any other covariates you include, such as batch.
Note: Some component values fall outside -1 to 1; read them as contributions, not correlations. Deciding which gene pairs differ beyond chance is a separate analysis.

The other registered options, and why they come later:
- **LIONESS-COEXPRESSION** — also fits, after the recommended: per-sample gene degree or edge weights can be compared between the groups or time points (paired when the same individuals give both).
- **BONOBO** — also fits, after the recommended: per-sample gene degree or edge weights can be compared between the groups or time points (paired when the same individuals give both).

